V59 Vita portable GX register/command decoder candidate, runtime default OFF.

Adapted from the 3DS port's patches/aurora/0009-3ds-fast-register-decode.patch.
Only portable register, colour, matrix/light and command parsing work is included.
No 3DS backend, verifier, PICA, shader-info reuse, or game simulation changes.

Apply after Vita Aurora 0001 and 0002 to Aurora
3227d76c60e1e782ca576610bce61c9e7744d8be. Pristine command_processor.cpp
SHA256 ff3eeb1c06562c0cbbeb5cbad0daa45aeb4370733dd073ccd34f10f6303ba5ab.
TWV_VITA_GX_FAST_DECODE defaults to 0. When compiled in, the frontend's locked
twv_vita_gx_fast_enabled() chooses original (0) or candidate (nonzero) at runtime.
OFF retains the original division/read_bits/store helpers and persistent ByteReader.
TWV_GX_DECODE_REF=1 compiles only the original implementations for an independent
namespace-remapped oracle. The candidate skips only writes the original handlers
ignore; mask, valid bits, triggers, DRAWDONE, viewport/projection and indexed-array
checks keep their original behavior. Short commands use the original reader errors.

